    <section class="rise-fall" id="timeline" aria-labelledby="timeline-title">
      <h2 class="profile-section-title" id="timeline-title">Timeline</h2>
      <ol class="rf-events"><li><span class="rf-year">c. 10th century BCE</span><span class="rf-text">By the biblical account, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">David</a> makes <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> his capital and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/solomon">Solomon</a> builds the First Temple</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">586 BCE</span><span class="rf-text">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylonians">Babylonians</a> destroy <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> and the First Temple and take many Judeans into exile</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">516 BCE</span><span class="rf-text">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/temple-in-jerusalem">Second Temple</a> is completed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> after the return from exile, by the traditional date</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">70</span><span class="rf-text">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> destroy <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/temple-in-jerusalem">Second Temple</a> at the end of the Jewish revolt</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">c. 200</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/judah">Judah</a> ha-Nasi compiles the Mishnah, the first great work of rabbinic law</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">c. 600</span><span class="rf-text">The Babylonian Talmud reaches its final form</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1492</span><span class="rf-text">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a> are expelled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1948</span><span class="rf-text">The State of Israel is founded, three years after the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holocaust">Holocaust</a></span></li></ol>
    </section>

